From ad3a707192ea414f56c125a0fb8b4348b2aca487 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:11:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Unified: fixes for the AI chat and the design check found by
 the AI's own testing, and optional auto-approve
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- run_python: undo changes in every document on errors and switch back to the document that was active;
  no undo step when nothing changed; added/removed objects are counted by events, not by names;
  a pattern made with Body.newObject that ends up after the Tip is made the Tip (as the GUI command does);
  a body with no visible step shows its Tip again
- run_python: sys.exit and KeyboardInterrupt are caught like other errors (sys.exit used to run FreeCAD's own
  shutdown and it crashed and hung); every run is logged to <user data>/ai/ai-runs.log (also before it runs); after three failures in
  a row the result tells the AI to change its approach or ask the user
- the AI is told not to start another FreeCAD (sys.executable is FreeCAD itself) and not to repeat failures
- get_document: step parameters (Type etc.) go into params instead of overwriting the object's type
- design check: steps after the Tip, bodies without a shape, hidden parts that were not checked;
  no free-DoF note while constraints conflict; constraint numbers are 1-based
- Japanese: the origin point is called 原点の点 (both were 原点)
- AI chat: optional auto-approve (off by default, not saved; the code that ran stays in the chat)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
